WaterUI Apple backend source provenance

This directory is the tracked source tree of the former
water-rs/apple-backend repository, imported without git ancestry
because that history contains commits a signed-ancestry repository
cannot accept. The original repository's full history is RETAINED by
water-rs/apple-backend; its archival is PENDING until this in-tree
import completes native acceptance — the old repository is not yet
archived.

Imported source — byte-identical to upstream merge `1c95fe2`:

  base tree:   34114ffc0e42caa99c4fee4814f840370402b424 (dev, PR #316)
  + delta:     cf47523188fa5b599d7c593f204f1f8a9e9e3cfe —
               "compile helpers only for their owning features",
               landed upstream as merge ef03d14 (PR #318)
  + delta:     b46de1d — "replay idle captured frames after context
               publication" (native-v7-followup), landed upstream as
               merge 1c95fe2 (PR #320)

The verified equivalence was established by diffing this tree against
`git archive 1c95fe2` — every tracked source file matches; the only
deliberate divergence is the two `waterui_path` values in
Examples/liquid_glass/Water.toml and Tests/IOSTestHost/Water.toml
(`../../..` → `../../../..`), corrected for the deeper in-tree
location.

Post-import integration: the typed Views-snapshot port for
List/Container/Table (water-rs/waterui#1418 adoption, apple side PR
#319, final v3) was applied in-tree by the primary worker at commit
`80978497` — `src/components/{list,container,table}.rs` and
`Tests/migration.rs` carry its source; the 308 single-invalidate
Container change is preserved verbatim within it.

Excluded from the import: Cargo.lock (the workspace lock owns
resolution), .github/ (CI migrated separately), .cargo/ and .config/
(member-level cargo/nextest config is inert under a root workspace —
the iOS-simulator runner and the bindgen triple fix moved into the root
.cargo/config.toml / .config/nextest.toml), Package.swift (moved to the repository root — the root Package.swift
is the single SwiftPM manifest) and the obsolete .swiftpm/ test scheme
(its WaterUITests target no longer exists; native tests live in Rust), and every generated or build output.

Imported text files without a terminal newline were normalized during
signed integration. No other source changes beyond those noted above.
